# Scopes the PmtcMail Docker build context (now the repo root, as of the
# 2026-08-31 switch to the real HTML-to-PDF mailer -- see
# infra/lib/mail-stack.ts) down to exactly what mailer/Dockerfile actually
# COPYs: mailer/generate.py, mailer/handler.py, output_report/. Without
# this, both CDK's own asset-hashing/staging step and the docker build
# itself have to walk the ENTIRE repo -- infra/node_modules/,
# infra/cdk.out/, .git (with LFS blobs), app/, tools/preview_output/,
# wireframe/ and all -- none of which the image needs. Added after that
# exact thing caused a deploy to stall for minutes with zero Docker
# activity, confirmed by `du` itself timing out on the repo root.
*
!mailer
!output_report
